course: dictionary
lesson: 6883
title: Override: a stronger power wins
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To override something is to cancel it because you have greater power or more importance. Override can be a verb, as in «to override a decision», or a noun, as in «an override», which is a switch or way to take control.
explain: «Congress can still override a veto if two-thirds of both parts vote again.» A veto is when a president says no to a bill, which is a plan for a new law. Here, override means the lawmakers can cancel that no, because they have enough votes to be the stronger power.
explain: Use the context clues. Ask yourself who has the bigger power and what is being cancelled. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: To override means to cancel something by using greater power.
fact: «Override» can also mean to be more important than something else, as in «safety overrides other rules».
fact: To override a machine means to stop it working automatically so that you can control it yourself.
fact: An override is a switch or way to do this, like a manual override.
fact: In the USA, a bill can be vetoed by the president, and Congress can override the veto if two-thirds of both the House and the Senate vote for it again.
exercise: «Congress can override a veto if two-thirds of both parts vote again.» What does override mean here? | Hold the bill up for a week | Make the bill shorter | *Cancel the veto using greater power | Sign the bill without any votes
exercise: The head of the school can override a teacher's decision. What does override mean? | Forget it on purpose | Agree with it happily | *Cancel it and make the final choice | Write it down on paper
exercise: In «a manual override» on a machine, what does the switch let you do? | Make the machine louder | Let the machine run on its own for ever | *Stop it working automatically and control it yourself | Turn the machine into a toy
test: In «safety overrides other rules», what does overrides mean? | *Is more important than | Breaks | Copies | Ignores the safety
test: In «an override», which word class is override? | *Noun | Adjective | Verb | Adverb
exam: «A veto is when a US president refuses to sign a bill; Congress can override it.» What does override tell us Congress can do to the veto? | Put it on a shelf | *Cancel it using greater power | Forget it | Accept it and sign it
